 "result_text": "`from_array()` in `pybboxes/boxes/base.py` now accepts an array with any number of leading dimensions, as long as the last one has length 4. Nested input gives back nested lists of box objects.\n\nI ran the example from the issue and a single box:\n- `CocoBoundingBox.from_array([[0,0,10,25],[5,3,16,24]])` returns a list of two `CocoBoundingBox` objects.\n- `CocoBoundingBox.from_array([1,2,3,4])` still returns a single box.\n\nI didn't run the test suite.\n\n- **Warning removed:** The `FutureWarning` about the method changing is gone, since the change has now happened.\n- **Stricter validation:** The check is now on the last dimension, so a scalar or any array whose last dimension isn't 4 raises a `ValueError`.\n- **Unused imports:** I left the `warnings` and `find_stack_level` imports in place, so they may now be unused.",
